WEBVTT

00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:10.590
Wiping off my tears.

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:13.300
I'm starting to run now

00:00:13.310 --> 00:00:18.560
Tomorrow I'll be born anew.

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:24.370
How could "you always be my friend"?

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:29.280
That person's word makes me more courageous.

00:00:29.290 --> 00:00:33.480
There are times when it's possible I will be depressed

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:38.580
and there are times when things are delightful.

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:45.170
I'll always be

00:00:46.130 --> 00:00:51.020
next to you.

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:55.910
Smiling 100%

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:59.450
Striking 100%

00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:03.640
I've come so far.

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:06.560
Being 100% pure

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:10.190
The things I want to tell you

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:14.670
change to treasure completely.

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:17.190
in the 100% case

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:20.950
Even if it's a long distance,

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:27.280
I'll still say I would meet you with the same feelings.

00:01:36.710 --> 00:01:43.240
Q-Class traveled to Jinchuumurato at Diet Member
Takatobi’s request, but he was dead on arrival.

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:48.700
He was found locked in his room, sealed from the inside by a concrete block.

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:52.870
Following his death, the CEO of Kagaki construction died as well.

00:01:52.890 --> 00:01:56.920
Goura was rumored to have been in collusion with Tobitaka.

00:01:57.690 --> 00:02:03.260
The police could not solve the case and it was declared a suicide.

00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:06.880
Get everyone together and prepare yourselves.

00:02:06.910 --> 00:02:08.840
We're going to face the real criminal!

00:02:16.170 --> 00:02:17.520
There are 3 hints.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:22.110
The first is the unnatural action of a certain person.

00:02:22.590 --> 00:02:26.440
The second is the method with which each fax arrived.

00:02:27.050 --> 00:02:33.450
The third is the vinyl sheet under the concrete block.

00:02:33.980 --> 00:02:35.870
There’s only one answer.

00:02:36.730 --> 00:02:38.160
Interesting.

00:02:38.190 --> 00:02:41.330
Let’s hear it then, DDS boy.

00:02:41.900 --> 00:02:46.970
First, what is the unnatural action that a certain person took?

00:02:47.530 --> 00:02:49.130
What certain person?

00:02:49.780 --> 00:02:50.590
The criminal.

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:56.640
The day after Goura-san was killed,

00:02:56.660 --> 00:02:59.810
we were washing our faces.

00:03:01.590 --> 00:03:04.690
Well, it’s complicated to explain.

00:03:04.710 --> 00:03:10.070
Kinta and I tried to sneak into the women’s bath to peek.

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:18.040
Meg saw me and threw everything she could find at us, bruising us all over.

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:22.420
And then this morning, Kinta’s face was swollen.

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:24.750
Actually, it was worse until a little while ago.

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:27.380
You don’t need to explain that!

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:28.880
Stupid.

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:31.590
I assumed you were just in a fight.

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:33.470
Did you think so too,

00:03:33.490 --> 00:03:34.800
Natsumi-san?

00:03:35.330 --> 00:03:36.470
No,

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:39.430
I just wondered what happened.

00:03:39.460 --> 00:03:41.600
Yes, that’s right.

00:03:41.630 --> 00:03:47.650
With a face as bruised as that, people would
normally assume he had got in a fight.

00:03:47.670 --> 00:03:51.570
People are usually curious regarding what happens.

00:03:51.590 --> 00:03:53.110
Don’t you agree?

00:03:53.140 --> 00:03:55.120
Y-Yeah.

00:03:55.140 --> 00:04:01.830
But there was one person who burst into laughter upon seeing his face.

00:04:02.860 --> 00:04:03.920
Right,

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:05.630
Hitsuki Yuri -san?

00:04:07.230 --> 00:04:08.960
What are you saying?

00:04:08.990 --> 00:04:10.300
I just.

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:14.140
No, you laughed.

00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:16.910
Oh, look at that face.

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:18.520
Don’t laugh!

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:20.600
By saying that, you agreed with me.

00:04:20.830 --> 00:04:23.310
Oh don’t worry, it’s his own fault.

00:04:23.330 --> 00:04:25.190
That’s' probably true!

00:04:25.840 --> 00:04:28.400
You said that and agreed with me.

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:31.110
I made a terrible mistake, you see.

00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:37.450
Yuri-san was with Kyuu and his company until just before the peeping incident,

00:04:37.470 --> 00:04:40.450
so I thought you were present the entire time.

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:46.420
In fact, you had left the bath and did not return that evening.

00:04:46.770 --> 00:04:51.090
So there’s no reason you would have normally laughed at Kinta’s face.

00:04:51.610 --> 00:04:55.050
It’s an extremely unnatural reaction.

00:04:55.620 --> 00:05:00.720
Yuri-san didn’t know we peeked, so where did she find that out?

00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:03.640
There was only one opportunity.

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:09.020
Around 10:45, when we walked past Goura’s room,

00:05:10.340 --> 00:05:13.700
that was what we were talking about.

00:05:14.260 --> 00:05:18.490
And at that time, the light in Goura’s room was off.

00:05:18.510 --> 00:05:22.330
He may have left the room in order to kill himself.

00:05:22.350 --> 00:05:23.790
I don’t think so.

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:32.170
He had just received a long fax from Natsumi-san a few minutes prior.

00:05:32.610 --> 00:05:33.520
Yes.

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:36.800
He was working in, his room.

00:05:36.820 --> 00:05:38.760
The time was around...

00:05:39.290 --> 00:05:42.100
The time recorded on the last page was

00:05:44.580 --> 00:05:46.520
10:30 PM.

00:05:47.170 --> 00:05:53.360
It’s hard to imagine that he’d ignore a fax
important enough to be sent late at night.

00:05:53.970 --> 00:05:55.150
Which means-

00:05:55.680 --> 00:05:59.030
the criminal was in the room at that time.

00:05:59.850 --> 00:06:04.750
And she heard us talking.

00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:09.330
That thing you hit us with was solid wood!

00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:12.840
It’s because you both were peeking. Jerks.

00:06:15.450 --> 00:06:17.050
That’s just...

00:06:17.070 --> 00:06:19.840
Just a hypothesis.

00:06:19.870 --> 00:06:23.720
I laughed cause it looked really funny!

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:26.020
That happens sometimes.

00:06:26.040 --> 00:06:27.390
Can you say it's impossible?

00:06:28.540 --> 00:06:30.560
No, we can’t.

00:06:30.590 --> 00:06:33.150
So we all looked for evidence

00:06:33.170 --> 00:06:37.110
to prove this hypothesis.

00:06:37.130 --> 00:06:38.860
Evidence?

00:06:38.890 --> 00:06:40.070
We found it.

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:46.790
While Kyuu, Meg and Kinta were in front of his
room it seems Goura-san still had energy left.

00:06:47.650 --> 00:06:49.540
“At this rate I'll be killed.”

00:06:49.560 --> 00:06:56.670
Goura realized this and used the last of his energy to write a message.

00:06:57.280 --> 00:07:00.510
We found the message hidden alongside the fax documents.

00:07:00.530 --> 00:07:02.550
That was one of the first things we investigated.

00:07:02.580 --> 00:07:04.350
Piece by piece.

00:07:04.370 --> 00:07:06.980
But there wasn’t anything there.

00:07:07.580 --> 00:07:09.350
Of course there wasn’t.

00:07:09.380 --> 00:07:16.860
The criminal would have found something as obvious as that and removed it.

00:07:17.380 --> 00:07:18.570
Goura-san thought the same thing:

00:07:19.470 --> 00:07:24.740
he wrote a message on the sides, rather than the front.

00:07:24.770 --> 00:07:29.870
He then scattered the papers around the room.

00:07:31.400 --> 00:07:34.040
Please, try and put it back in order.

00:07:38.530 --> 00:07:39.550
We're done.

00:07:44.200 --> 00:07:45.180
Kashiya?

00:07:45.830 --> 00:07:48.140
Those are the people who sent this fax.

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:49.810
Kashiya Design Offices.

00:07:50.460 --> 00:07:53.560
But why is “ya” the only character in hiragana?

00:07:53.590 --> 00:07:55.360
No!

00:07:55.380 --> 00:07:57.030
That’s not it, detective.

00:07:58.260 --> 00:07:59.490
Lend it to me.

00:08:00.180 --> 00:08:01.320
I knew it.

00:08:01.340 --> 00:08:03.820
You ordered it beginning from the first page.

00:08:03.850 --> 00:08:04.870
Hey!

00:08:05.310 --> 00:08:08.160
The faxes here come in reverse order.

00:08:08.850 --> 00:08:12.170
They come out on top of the other.

00:08:12.980 --> 00:08:16.420
The faxes at HQ are like that too.

00:08:16.440 --> 00:08:18.130
Is that so?

00:08:18.150 --> 00:08:21.300
So when it arrived, the order was like...

00:08:21.320 --> 00:08:27.060
Natsumi-san, when you delivered this to Goura,
you didn’t reorder it or anything did you?

00:08:27.790 --> 00:08:28.720
No,

00:08:28.750 --> 00:08:31.100
I just took what was there.

00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:32.480
I knew it.

00:08:32.500 --> 00:08:33.390
Just as I thought.

00:08:35.460 --> 00:08:37.730
Here you go, it’s done.

00:08:37.760 --> 00:08:40.230
Now what does it say?

00:08:41.470 --> 00:08:42.490
You can read it right?

00:08:42.510 --> 00:08:43.200
It says Hitsuki.

00:08:43.220 --> 00:08:44.160
What?

00:08:48.470 --> 00:08:50.410
This is the second hint.

00:08:50.430 --> 00:08:52.290
The way the fax arrives.

00:08:52.310 --> 00:08:57.340
We were surprised that the characters changed
if you line the paper up in reverse.

00:08:57.360 --> 00:09:03.510
But we were even more surprised when they looked like the
name of the sender when lined up in the wrong order!

00:09:04.620 --> 00:09:06.550
This is a trap.

00:09:08.080 --> 00:09:11.140
A trap set by,Goura as he killed himself.

00:09:11.160 --> 00:09:16.150
He tried to set me up before he committed suicide!

00:09:17.130 --> 00:09:18.900
What do you mean?

00:09:24.680 --> 00:09:26.660
I was his lover.

00:09:26.680 --> 00:09:27.620
What?

00:09:29.010 --> 00:09:30.410
What did you say?

00:09:30.930 --> 00:09:36.670
It seemed as if the corruption affiliated behind
this case was about to be made public,

00:09:36.690 --> 00:09:40.170
so I went and said my goodbyes.

00:09:40.190 --> 00:09:42.840
And then this happened.

00:09:42.860 --> 00:09:46.090
He was really in trouble.

00:09:46.120 --> 00:09:48.930
That’s impossible!

00:09:48.950 --> 00:09:54.480
You didn’t look like that kind of person at all
when you were visiting your boyfriend’s grave.

00:09:55.170 --> 00:09:59.110
You can’t judge a book by it’s cover.

00:09:59.130 --> 00:10:05.780
Ah, yes. I'll admit that I was in Goura's room when you passed by.

00:10:12.560 --> 00:10:15.910
Don’t make such an obvious lie, please.

00:10:16.520 --> 00:10:18.460
But it does make sense.

00:10:19.110 --> 00:10:19.880
See?

00:10:19.900 --> 00:10:23.250
It would appear to be DDS that doesn’t make any sense.

00:10:23.780 --> 00:10:28.340
How was I supposed to kill him in the first place?

00:10:28.370 --> 00:10:30.470
No, not just me.

00:10:31.120 --> 00:10:37.230
It’s impossible to murder someone in a locked room and escape!

00:10:38.210 --> 00:10:46.940
Because the locked room murder was so perfect, it doesn’t
matter if the other murder and suicide are fakes.

00:10:47.680 --> 00:10:48.990
That’s what you thought?

00:10:50.550 --> 00:10:59.330
You're right: as long as the mystery of that locked room is unsolved,
the only course of action is to declare it an accident or a suicide

00:10:59.980 --> 00:11:03.590
But you know, it’s all over.

00:11:04.900 --> 00:11:08.130
Your final fortress has crumbled.

00:11:08.740 --> 00:11:10.010
What?

00:11:10.570 --> 00:11:12.680
Kid!

00:11:12.700 --> 00:11:15.390
Are you saying you solved the mystery of that locked room?

00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:16.970
Yes.

00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:18.600
I'll show you how it was done at the scene.

00:11:22.670 --> 00:11:26.900
I’m going to recreate the locked room murder.

00:11:26.920 --> 00:11:27.900
Please observe.

00:11:28.430 --> 00:11:31.450
This is the way the inside looked at the time.

00:11:32.220 --> 00:11:35.120
There were only two windows and both of them were locked.

00:11:35.770 --> 00:11:40.330
The one door leading to the interior was being obstructed

00:11:40.350 --> 00:11:45.290
by a huge concrete block from the inside.

00:11:45.320 --> 00:11:48.760
I pulled the door out with the construction vehicle.

00:11:49.660 --> 00:11:51.340
I fixed it.

00:11:51.370 --> 00:11:53.720
As you can see, it now closes.

00:12:00.920 --> 00:12:02.150
It doesn’t open.

00:12:02.170 --> 00:12:03.860
Did you lock it or something?

00:12:05.340 --> 00:12:09.860
There’s a large mass blocking it from the inside, just as we first found it.

00:12:11.470 --> 00:12:16.780
With a the doors and windows shut, how did
you manage to block the door from the inside?

00:12:17.600 --> 00:12:19.120
There’s only one way.

00:12:19.890 --> 00:12:22.670
The same way the criminal did it.

00:12:23.230 --> 00:12:25.130
That’s the 3rd hint.

00:12:25.150 --> 00:12:28.590
The vinyl sheet under the concrete block.

00:12:29.700 --> 00:12:31.920
I'll recreate this scene.

00:12:32.490 --> 00:12:33.180
Yuri-san,

00:12:34.490 --> 00:12:39.350
how did you create a perfect locked room murder?

00:12:39.830 --> 00:12:43.190
The brilliant trick behind it all is-

00:12:55.300 --> 00:13:00.830
Detective Mine, would you take down the tape and open the door?

00:13:02.060 --> 00:13:03.210
Here you go.

00:13:19.330 --> 00:13:19.970
Here.

00:13:24.580 --> 00:13:25.390
What?

00:13:25.420 --> 00:13:27.270
That’s just cardboard!

00:13:27.840 --> 00:13:29.900
Not just cardboard.

00:13:30.460 --> 00:13:34.900
In order to block,the door it’s been sealed with vinyl and filled with water.

00:13:37.180 --> 00:13:38.280
This is how it’s done.

00:13:39.510 --> 00:13:44.410
Put a vinyl bag on the inside of the cardboard
before opening the door and leaving.

00:13:44.440 --> 00:13:50.170
Place it in the foyer, open the door and walk outside.

00:13:50.190 --> 00:13:55.630
Then, pull the string attached to the cardboard, pulling it to the dirt floor.

00:13:56.160 --> 00:13:59.850
Then, using a rubber hose from the fan vent,

00:13:59.870 --> 00:14:02.060
put water in the cardboard box.

00:14:02.750 --> 00:14:04.930
This becomes a weight that blocks the door

00:14:05.540 --> 00:14:07.230
So what?

00:14:07.250 --> 00:14:11.730
It wasn't a cardboard box blocking the door, it was a huge concrete block.

00:14:13.970 --> 00:14:16.320
That was the trick that fooled us.

00:14:17.430 --> 00:14:21.280
In other words, she didn’t move that heavy concrete block.

00:14:22.310 --> 00:14:26.290
Just like with the water, she lowered liquid
concrete in where it dried and solidified!

00:14:28.520 --> 00:14:29.710
Inside this?

00:14:30.150 --> 00:14:32.250
The concrete became solid...

00:14:35.360 --> 00:14:39.510
Modern concrete begins to dry in about eight hours.

00:14:39.530 --> 00:14:43.640
After 24, it will  be tough enough to support a car.

00:14:44.250 --> 00:14:50.600
Since those were nearby, we all thought it was taken from there.

00:14:51.090 --> 00:14:52.690
But the box,

00:14:52.710 --> 00:14:54.570
what did they do about the box then?

00:14:55.260 --> 00:14:56.490
Burned it!

00:14:57.010 --> 00:15:00.990
After the concrete hardened, the proof was concealed.

00:15:01.430 --> 00:15:05.830
But that alone would be suspicious, so she set fire to the body too.

00:15:06.480 --> 00:15:10.000
Setting it to follow the legend of Mayahime’s Hitobashira.

00:15:10.730 --> 00:15:15.630
But there was one part that she couldn’t do anything about, the bottom.

00:15:16.280 --> 00:15:21.050
After the concrete had hardened, the vinyl on the bottom couldn’t be burnt.

00:15:22.030 --> 00:15:28.020
So, she used a sheet from the construction site
that wouldn’t appear suspicious when found.

00:15:28.620 --> 00:15:32.650
The vinyl sheets on top of that pile of sand were the same color,

00:15:33.170 --> 00:15:34.320
so I figured it out.

00:15:36.670 --> 00:15:37.610
Yuri-san,

00:15:38.260 --> 00:15:39.320
it’s over.

00:15:39.890 --> 00:15:42.780
Just admit it.

00:15:43.310 --> 00:15:44.950
No way.

00:15:44.970 --> 00:15:51.040
Yuri-san, there has to be a reason that somebody like you did that!

00:15:51.060 --> 00:15:51.790
Right?

00:15:56.570 --> 00:15:57.840
You're right

00:15:57.860 --> 00:15:59.300
I did it.

00:15:59.860 --> 00:16:02.340
I killed those two.

00:16:02.870 --> 00:16:04.260
No way,

00:16:04.280 --> 00:16:06.350
you were a traitor.

00:16:06.910 --> 00:16:08.640
You’re wrong Musashi.

00:16:09.160 --> 00:16:15.310
In order to continue fighting against the dam’s
construction, which began with her lover,

00:16:16.050 --> 00:16:17.780
she deliberately became his secretary

00:16:19.380 --> 00:16:21.650
He’s right, Musashi-kun.

00:16:21.680 --> 00:16:23.490
That was my goal.

00:16:23.500 --> 00:16:26.120
But it didn’t work at all!

00:16:27.430 --> 00:16:32.080
No matter how much data I gathered, no matter how
much I tried to persuade him against the construction,

00:16:32.100 --> 00:16:34.830
it didn’t matter. They wouldn’t listen to me!

00:16:36.020 --> 00:16:42.930
Money was their only excuse for drowning this village!

00:16:42.950 --> 00:16:45.970
Then, that was your motive?

00:16:47.910 --> 00:16:57.520
Hey, Musashi-kun, you said it was as if Takatobi
and Goura had killed your brother, right?

00:16:57.550 --> 00:16:59.570
Yeah.

00:16:59.590 --> 00:17:02.450
If they hadn’t built that dam,

00:17:02.470 --> 00:17:05.570
then he would never have opposed the construction.

00:17:05.600 --> 00:17:08.490
He never would’ve been in that accident.

00:17:09.520 --> 00:17:10.950
It wasn’t an accident!

00:17:13.150 --> 00:17:15.290
It wasn’t an accident.

00:17:15.310 --> 00:17:19.130
They made it look like one, but it was murder!

00:17:21.490 --> 00:17:23.670
Well, everything turned out all right.

00:17:23.700 --> 00:17:29.510
But Sensei, I was worried when you got into a fight
with him. Could you have pushed him off a cliff?

00:17:29.540 --> 00:17:30.560
Well, maybe.

00:17:31.080 --> 00:17:35.810
But thanks to his death, we are now proceeding much smoother.

00:17:35.830 --> 00:17:39.610
Hitobashira generally come with dam construction, huh?

00:17:45.890 --> 00:17:47.110
How awful.

00:17:47.140 --> 00:17:48.490
That means-

00:17:48.510 --> 00:17:53.330
If that was the case, then you should’ve come to the police!

00:17:53.350 --> 00:17:54.250
Why?

00:17:54.730 --> 00:17:55.790
“Why?”

00:17:57.020 --> 00:17:58.580
I didn’t have any proof.

00:17:59.230 --> 00:18:04.800
And even if they were caught, it wouldn’t have quelled my anger.

00:18:05.740 --> 00:18:09.140
I decided to burn anyone who tried to destroy our village for his own benefit,

00:18:10.080 --> 00:18:15.020
using the power of the village’s guardian Mayahime.

00:18:16.420 --> 00:18:17.190
What are you doing?

00:18:17.210 --> 00:18:21.770
So ever since this idea was given to me, I decided.

00:18:22.050 --> 00:18:22.900
“Given to her"?

00:18:23.880 --> 00:18:24.740
Pluto!

00:18:25.510 --> 00:18:29.910
That even if I succeeded, I would go to him.

00:18:30.430 --> 00:18:34.660
The final Hitobashira that will,protect this village is me!

00:18:35.230 --> 00:18:36.160
Stop it!

00:18:36.730 --> 00:18:37.460
Yuri-san!

00:18:45.360 --> 00:18:46.880
Yuri-san!

00:18:49.990 --> 00:18:50.720
Kinta!

00:18:50.740 --> 00:18:51.470
Oh no!

00:18:57.000 --> 00:18:58.060
Yuri-san!

00:18:58.830 --> 00:19:00.810
Jinnai-san.

00:19:00.840 --> 00:19:01.810
Hypnosis.

00:19:04.510 --> 00:19:05.480
Hey, you guys.

00:19:05.510 --> 00:19:06.780
Get an ambulance.

00:19:06.800 --> 00:19:08.070
Right!

00:19:08.090 --> 00:19:08.820
Kinta!

00:19:08.840 --> 00:19:09.820
Are you OK?

00:19:09.840 --> 00:19:10.910
Yeah.

00:19:10.930 --> 00:19:12.990
What happened?

00:19:18.690 --> 00:19:19.620
That man is

00:19:19.650 --> 00:19:20.670
Obana-san?

00:19:20.690 --> 00:19:21.460
What?

00:19:26.280 --> 00:19:28.760
Could that just now have been-

00:19:28.780 --> 00:19:29.760
Pluto.

00:19:30.240 --> 00:19:31.340
What?

00:19:31.370 --> 00:19:33.850
Damn, they got away?

00:19:35.120 --> 00:19:36.270
My my!

00:19:36.960 --> 00:19:39.140
I've gotta go back and report this.

00:19:39.920 --> 00:19:40.940
Jinnai -san.

00:19:42.290 --> 00:19:45.480
You're with DDS, aren’t you?

00:19:50.510 --> 00:19:55.080
Seeing through my disguise, Q-Class is much more skilled than before.

00:19:55.100 --> 00:19:56.120
What?

00:19:58.890 --> 00:20:01.170
At one time, I was the reporter Jinnai Takuma.

00:20:02.230 --> 00:20:04.340
Another time I was the waiter for Ryozanpaku,

00:20:04.980 --> 00:20:07.550
the inn in Hyoutanmura Kirihara Masaya.

00:20:07.570 --> 00:20:11.880
And another time, the butler for the Ichinose family, Ootaburo Tamotsu.

00:20:12.570 --> 00:20:14.850
I was also Gejira and Karuizawa!

00:20:14.870 --> 00:20:15.800
Panda!

00:20:15.830 --> 00:20:16.810
Cactus!

00:20:18.660 --> 00:20:23.770
But my true identity would be the one who supervises DDS from the shadows,

00:20:25.210 --> 00:20:31.650
the right hand of Dan Morihiko, Nanami Gotarou!

00:20:34.760 --> 00:20:43.040
You had a request from the real Jinnai to reveal the
corruption behind Takatobi and Kagaki construction?

00:20:43.060 --> 00:20:44.210
Yeah.

00:20:44.230 --> 00:20:48.250
I was surprised when you guys showed up.

00:20:48.280 --> 00:20:54.840
That makes sense. Since you were here, Hongou relaxed and went back to DDS.

00:20:54.870 --> 00:20:56.390
That’s correct.

00:20:56.410 --> 00:21:02.020
You wouldn’t need two of DDS’s best detectives supervising Q-Class.

00:21:02.790 --> 00:21:04.190
Oh, don’t flatter me.

00:21:04.830 --> 00:21:10.320
But two jobs after the same crime is quite a coincidence.

00:21:11.260 --> 00:21:13.610
I hope that’s all it is.

00:21:14.390 --> 00:21:18.950
Why did Hongou-sensei leave the crime scene without investigating?

00:21:18.970 --> 00:21:20.540
That’s who he is.

00:21:20.560 --> 00:21:23.290
There must have been some reason.

00:21:23.310 --> 00:21:25.080
I wonder.

00:21:25.610 --> 00:21:28.000
It may just be my imagination,

00:21:28.020 --> 00:21:32.800
but ever since his wounds healed upon returning to DDS,

00:21:32.820 --> 00:21:36.930
Hongou-sensei’s actions have become suspicious.

00:21:39.410 --> 00:21:43.680
I'll go see if there’s been any kind of contact from him.

00:22:04.640 --> 00:22:05.330
Ryuu-sama.

00:22:06.060 --> 00:22:07.460
Anubis.

00:22:07.480 --> 00:22:09.790
Stop following me!

00:22:10.440 --> 00:22:12.880
So your decision remains unchanged?

00:22:12.900 --> 00:22:16.970
Tell King Hades that from this point on, we're enemies.

00:22:17.910 --> 00:22:19.090
Are you certain?

00:22:19.120 --> 00:22:20.600
I am.

00:22:27.290 --> 00:22:31.690
I have no choice but to set my last resort into action, Ryuu-sama.

00:22:35.260 --> 00:22:37.450
Thank you very much.

00:22:37.470 --> 00:22:39.660
If you’d like, you can come again.

00:22:39.680 --> 00:22:42.870
Sure! If you really wanted me to, I'd be glad to come again.

00:22:43.850 --> 00:22:44.950
I don't really.

00:22:46.810 --> 00:22:49.540
But Ryuu’s late.

00:22:59.410 --> 00:23:00.470
Ryuu-kun.

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:02.760
I’m sorry.

00:23:02.790 --> 00:23:04.850
I ruined your bike.

00:23:05.710 --> 00:23:08.730
No, it was a mess from the start.

00:23:09.330 --> 00:23:11.020
Come on , take my had.

00:23:13.840 --> 00:23:16.650
You seem different from usual, Ryuu.

00:23:16.670 --> 00:23:17.900
You think?

00:23:19.800 --> 00:23:22.490
Has he changed a bit?

00:23:22.510 --> 00:23:24.240
There’s something very strange going on.

00:23:25.810 --> 00:23:28.500
Come on, the crime’s been solved.

00:23:28.520 --> 00:23:29.830
Let’s get back to DDS.

00:23:30.400 --> 00:23:31.830
Yeah!

00:23:34.400 --> 00:23:35.800
That much.

00:23:35.820 --> 00:23:37.130
Is it OK?

00:23:37.150 --> 00:23:41.340
Yeah, try and stir up DDS.

00:23:47.860 --> 00:23:51.770
Somehow it's collapsing

00:23:51.800 --> 00:23:54.140
Embracing such a feeling.

00:23:54.160 --> 00:23:55.030
Flowing.

00:23:55.050 --> 00:23:58.910
I'd be worried tomorrow.

00:23:58.930 --> 00:24:01.120
If the same thing happened.

00:24:01.140 --> 00:24:02.120
Go wrong.

00:24:02.130 --> 00:24:06.460
He looks up at the sky, pondering

00:24:06.470 --> 00:24:09.020
You're very far away.

00:24:09.930 --> 00:24:13.180
Show your heart if you have the courage

00:24:13.190 --> 00:24:16.310
passing the border line.

00:24:16.330 --> 00:24:19.760
In order to get past, I walk against the wind

00:24:19.770 --> 00:24:23.400
and I can finish a battle.

00:24:23.420 --> 00:24:26.940
When I feel like an abandoned child

00:24:26.970 --> 00:24:30.360
then I'll stand in line with you.

00:24:30.390 --> 00:24:33.930
Facing the wind, I forget,

00:24:33.940 --> 00:24:37.540
somehow this is the only important thing.

00:24:37.550 --> 00:24:40.290
We protect, because there Is no return.

00:24:40.310 --> 00:24:41.890
It's becoming dearly.

00:24:41.920 --> 00:24:45.840
Today I embrace, right now I conquer.

00:24:46.800 --> 00:24:56.000
Next Episode

00:24:47.390 --> 00:24:49.160
Dan Morihiko is kidnapped, and the man responsible

00:24:49.180 --> 00:24:51.830
demands five hundred million yen by sundown.

00:24:51.850 --> 00:24:55.670
All of the members of DDS band together in a daring rescue,

00:24:55.690 --> 00:24:59.050
but the culprit is already aware of our movements.

00:24:59.070 --> 00:25:00.630
There’s been a leak!

00:25:00.650 --> 00:25:03.550
Could it be that there’s a spy n DDS?

00:25:03.570 --> 00:25:04.640
There is only one answer!

00:25:08.200 --> 00:25:09.810
What’s wrong, Kinta?

00:25:11.210 --> 00:25:13.520
Farewell, Yuri-san.

00:25:15.000 --> 00:25:19.080
Farewell, my 37th first love.

00:25:19.080 --> 00:25:21.670
I don't think that's still first love...
